@FG-K0-6bc04e6316 CORRECT conf=M cls=CLASSIFICATION
why: The check errors when Directory.Packages.props lacks the property. CPM enabled in Directory.Build.props satisfies DEP-006 and is still reported as an error, so the check is broader than the policy. C3 treats a broader match set as a workflow remainder, not a coverage detail. DEP-023 prefers the packages file but is DEFAULT, so it does not close the gap.
q: .claude/scripts/check-dependencies.cjs:167-170 | ManagePackageVersionsCentrally must be true
set classification=CANONICAL_PLUS_DELTA
set oracle_relation=PARTIALLY_ENTAILED
set strength_vs_canonical=STRONGER
set extra_fragment_kind=EXTRA_WORKFLOW
set extra_fragment=The checker requires ManagePackageVersionsCentrally=true inside Directory.Packages.props itself.
set distinguishing_scenario=CPM is enabled in Directory.Build.props and the packages file has no such property: DEP-006 is met; the K0 checker reports an error.
amb: Read statically. A checker runs only when invoked. Most repositories set the property in the packages file, so the practical effect is small.

